==============================================================================
 (A) CF(n/Phi_6(n)) = [0; n-1, n]
==============================================================================
   n=3: 3/7 -> CF [0, 2, 3]   (= [0, n-1=2, n=3])
   n=5: 5/21 -> CF [0, 4, 5]   (= [0, n-1=4, n=5])
   n=7: 7/43 -> CF [0, 6, 7]   (= [0, n-1=6, n=7])
   n=14: 14/183 -> CF [0, 13, 14]   (= [0, n-1=13, n=14])

==============================================================================
 (B) THREE-DISTANCE: binding config {1..12,182}*14 mod 183 -- the gaps
==============================================================================
   runner positions: [14, 28, 42, 56, 70, 84, 98, 112, 126, 140, 154, 168, 169]
   gaps (Counter): {1: 1, 14: 11, 28: 1}  -> 3 distinct (three-distance: <=3)
   largest gap = 28; observer 0 sits in it; M = (largest gap)/2 / D = 14/183 = 0.07650
   (= 14/183, the covering-min; the deep hole is the half of the size-28 gap around 0)

==============================================================================
 (C) TORUS LIFT: Eisenstein reps of the speeds in Z[w]/(14-w), |a+bw|^2=a^2+ab+b^2
==============================================================================
   speed -> Eisenstein rep (a,b), norm:
       1 -> (  1, 0)  norm   1  [on the a-axis line, b=0]
       2 -> (  2, 0)  norm   4  [on the a-axis line, b=0]
       3 -> (  3, 0)  norm   9  [on the a-axis line, b=0]
       4 -> (  4, 0)  norm  16  [on the a-axis line, b=0]
       5 -> (  5, 0)  norm  25  [on the a-axis line, b=0]
       6 -> (  6, 0)  norm  36  [on the a-axis line, b=0]
       7 -> ( -7, 1)  norm  43
       8 -> ( -6, 1)  norm  31
       9 -> ( -5, 1)  norm  21
      10 -> ( -4, 1)  norm  13
      11 -> ( -3, 1)  norm   7
      12 -> ( -2, 1)  norm   3
     182 -> ( -1, 0)  norm   1  [on the a-axis line, b=0]
   => 7/13 speeds lie on the a-axis (b=0): the speed set is a LINE in the hexagonal lattice.
   so the covering-min is a 1D LINE in the 2D hexagonal lattice; the three-gap (B) governs the line,
   and the 3 gaps are the line's view of the 3 hexagonal nearest-neighbor directions (the A2 3-fold).
